=== layout: title-slide

# Lecture 08F

## Three-Point Test-Cross Worked Example

## Chapter 8

## Dr. Neil Voss

## October 27, 2026


=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Identify parental genotypes from offspring counts.
- Classify recombinants one gene pair at a time.
- Calculate all three pairwise recombination frequencies.
- Determine gene order and place map intervals.


=== layout: two-panels

# &#x1FAB0; Fruit Fly Inheritance

@left

- *C: chummy* - stays close to other flies.
- *D: dewy* - has moisture droplets on its body.
- *H: horsey* - is unusually large and strong-looking.
- Lowercase letters identify recessive alleles; + means wild type.

@right

![A triple heterozygote crossed with a recessive tester, with each locus listed separately.](assets/lect08f-three_point_testcross_bpw/testcross.svg)

Offspring phenotypes reveal the heterozygote's gametes.

@citation

Fictional fruit-fly traits; gene order is not yet known.


