# Does the Pair Match Either Parent?

@body

![Two green parental references, c+ and +d, above offspring cd+ (120) and c+h (75); H is covered and P/R answers are withheld.](assets/lect08f-three_point_testcross_bpw/classify_cd_question.svg)


=== layout: one-panel

# Match the Pair, Not the Count

@body

![cd matches neither parent and is recombinant; c+ matches the first parent and is parental for C-D despite its different H allele.](assets/lect08f-three_point_testcross_bpw/classify_cd_answer.svg)

@citation

Counts identify the original parents. Allele combinations classify the other rows.


