=== layout: section

# Summary


=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Start with the two most frequent offspring classes.
- Cover one gene and classify each remaining pair separately.
- Sum recombinants, divide by total offspring, and multiply by 100.
- Use all three results to place the genes.
- Double crossovers can make outer-pair recombination smaller than the mapped interval sum.


